---
// <BcnDividerTabs> — a page's views as tabs centered on the divider under its title (2026-10-28, Andy: "the big tabs
// at the top right are too big, not scalable. Can we introduce a new pattern of centered tabs through the divider.
// Make tabs a step smaller."). The rule runs the page's width and the tabs sit on it, so the views read as what the
// page is cut into, not as one more control in the title row, and the row holds more of them than the title's right
// edge did. The page puts its esa-button-toggle (size sm) in the slot and keeps driving it; the host page drops its
// title row's own divider (this is that divider).
//
// bcn-lego-checked: the tabs ARE esa-button-toggle (slotted; this component never touches it). No esa- lego is a rule
// with a control centered on it; checked Beacon (prod pages put tabs in a header row or a tab layout). The CSS is the
// rule and the centering.
---

<div class="bcn-dtabs">
  <span class="bcn-dtabs__rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <span class="bcn-dtabs__tabs"><slot /></span>
  <span class="bcn-dtabs__rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
</div>

<style>
  .bcn-dtabs {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(var(--spacing-400), 1fr) auto minmax(var(--spacing-400), 1fr);
    align-items: center;
    column-gap: var(--spacing-300);
  }
  .bcn-dtabs__rule {
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--color-border-default);
  }
  .bcn-dtabs__tabs {
    display: inline-flex;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .bcn-dtabs__tabs :global([hidden]) {
    display: none;
  }
</style>
